; an `alias` declares its name, as `infix` or `const` do: a symbol is declared by one file only.
; prop.kurt's `alias ∧ and` and modal.kurt's constructor `∧` (an object-level connective) were
; loaded together without an error, and `∧` then silently meant prop's meta-level `and`
; (found by the consistency check of 2026-10-09).
load modal
expect "EvalError" "declared in `modal.kurt` and in `prop.kurt`"
    load prop
